          "image_source": "images/page_15_image_10.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.232,
            0.503,
            0.426,
            0.523
          ],
          "content": "Multiplication fact:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.232,
            0.529,
            0.8,
            0.55
          ],
          "content": "Compare your picture and answers with your classmates!"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.556,
            0.885,
            0.617
          ],
          "content": "2. Draw a picture to show how much each child gets when 2 rotis are shared equally by 4 children. Also, write the corresponding division facts, addition facts, and multiplication facts."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.205,
            0.623,
            0.885,
            0.664
          ],
          "content": "3. Anil was in a group where 2 cakes were divided equally among 5   children. How much cake would Anil get?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.711,
            0.44,
            0.811
          ],
          "content": "Now, if there are 10 children in my group, how many cakes will I need so that they get same amount of cake as Anil?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.567,
            0.694,
            0.839,
            0.815
          ],
          "content": "What if we put two such groups together? one group where 2 cakes are divided equally between 5 children, and another group again with 4 cakes and 10 children."
        },
